       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify a dose that high. It raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI and bleeding effects.\n\nPlease check these points:\n- **Typo or unit error:** Did you mean 100 mg or 200 mg, or 40 mg?\n- **Usual dosing:**\n  - Depression, anxiety, PTSD: start at 25\u201350 mg daily and titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least one week, up to 200 mg/day.\n  - OCD: start at 50 mg daily, up to 200 mg/day.\n- **Intentional supratherapeutic dose:** If a supervising physician or psychiatrist has deliberately chosen this, I'll need that confirmation and the rationale. I can then enter the order with a note, though pharmacy will probably still review it.\n\nPlease talk to your resident or attending, and tell me the dose you want. I'll enter it right away. If it's a standard dose, for example 50 mg PO once daily, I can add a note with the indication."
